ks: US tariffs, threats to Greenland, the Iran war's economic effects. The government survived the subsequent no-confidence vote; coalition discipline held. But the admission marks a break. For three years the government had attributed poor performance to external factors while maintaining its target commitments. That defence has now been publicly abandoned. The Finance Ministry projects debt reaching 99% of GDP by 2030. Riikka Purra, the finance minister, maintained the consolidation course and attributed rising poverty almost entirely to immigration; Tytti Tuppurainen, who leads the SDP parliamentary group, called it \"Europe's worst economic management.\"\n\nAn academic survey published this week set the public backdrop in sharper relief. Some 73% of Finns would still vote for NATO membership and 80% say it has increased their security — but trust in the United States has effectively collapsed. About 80% say they cannot trust Washington to defend European allies, 80% want to reduce dependence on US weapons and technology, and only one-quarter trust the bilateral defence cooperation agreement. Only one-third now see NATO as a liberal democratic community, down from nearly half a year ago. The researchers described their findings as \"tense\" with government messaging. With Finland locked into the F-35 for 40 years, the public has recognised a dependency the government has no near-term way to dissolve. Karelian Sword 26 — 10,000 troops, with US and UK participation — begins May 18.",
